        <span itemprop="subject">the nonaqueous secondary battery separator in accordance with Comparative Example 17</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">was immersed for 24 hours in an electrolyte solution at 25° C. which was obtained by dissolving LiPF 6 with a concentration of 1.0 mole per liter in a mixed solvent of ethyl methyl carbonate, diethyl carbonate, and ethylene carbonate in a volume ratio of 50:20:30. After the immersion for 24 hours, in the porous layer including the ethylene-vinyl acetate copolymer-based resin, the resin having absorbed the electrolyte solution had a volume of 12 cm 3 per square meter of the porous layer.</span>
